MID_EV13_020_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_020_m01_001: An interesting match. This alone would have been\nworth the voyage here.
MID_EV13_020_m01_002: Just so. Both combatants were incredibly skilled.
MID_EV13_020_m01_003: That's the caliber of match we can expect to see\nhere in the seat of the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV13_020_m01_004: Yeah, they were some tough customers. Even\nSaramis doesn't have many like those two.
MID_EV13_020_m01_005: <NCA>Think back on the match.
MID_EV13_020_m01_006: That one they called the White-Maned Demon lost\nin the end, but his technique was unparalleled.
MID_EV13_020_m01_007: He must have devoted himself to study under\na master to attain such skill.
MID_EV13_020_m01_008: This is the Divine Sovereign's city, not mine. But it\nseems a waste for that man to remain a gladiator.
MID_EV13_020_m01_009: It makes me wonder what circumstances led to him\nfighting in such a miserable pit.
MID_EV13_020_m01_010: That Cruaidín also intrigued me. He surpassed even\nthe White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV13_020_m01_011: One thing baffles me on that point.
MID_EV13_020_m01_012: That man Cruaidín. I am told he is a warrior from\nthe kingdom of Brezarant.
MID_EV13_020_m01_013: His battle scars and experience would suggest that\nhe is a well-tested veteran.
MID_EV13_020_m01_014: Meaning he ought to have a long and storied career\nbehind him, no?
MID_EV13_020_m01_015: So I find it strange that I have never heard the\nslightest mention of him.
MID_EV13_020_m01_016: There you go, Bona, taking a hundred words to\nsay a single thing.
MID_EV13_020_m01_017: Just be brave enough to admit you're embarrassed\nnot to have heard of the guy.
MID_EV13_020_m01_018: Tobias! That was not my intent at all. What I was\ntrying to say was—
MID_EV13_020_m01_019: He fights under an alias. For whatever reason, he\nseeks to protect his identity.
MID_EV13_020_m01_020: I don't get it, boss. What would be the point?
MID_EV13_020_m01_021: To answer that, we would need knowledge of his\nidentity, motives, and goals.
MID_EV13_020_m01_022: Consider that there is another mystery surrounding\nCruaidín and the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV13_020_m01_023: I suspect that they both learned the art of war from\nthe same source.
MID_EV13_020_m01_024: The styles were different, but the fundamentals,\ntheir footwork and breathing... I saw it at once.
MID_EV13_020_m01_025: And? What's that mean for us?
MID_EV13_020_m01_026: I don't know. But I believe these two were matched\nin the arena for a reason.
MID_EV13_020_m01_027: Look into the combatants, Bonaventure. I would\nknow more of them both.
MID_EV13_065_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_065_m01_001: I'm Anna, an attendant priest in Solel's temple.\nI'm helping to oversee the Heroic Games.
MID_EV13_065_m01_002: I hope the day finds you well, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_065_m01_003: There's no need for such formality. You were at the\nDivine Sovereign's side during our audience, yes?
MID_EV13_065_m01_004: <NCA>Observe Anna.
MID_EV13_065_m01_005: <NCB>Hear her out.
MID_EV13_065_m01_006: <ACA>I somehow doubt any "attendant priest" would be so\nclose to the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_065_m01_007: <ACA>Well, well. You noticed that, hmm? Keep it to\nyourself, please.
MID_EV13_065_m01_008: The Dagsion Heroic Games are to be held over\nthe next half year.
MID_EV13_065_m01_009: We hope this display of martial excellence will stir\nDagda the Great to awaken.
MID_EV13_065_m01_010: More than three thousand clans will participate. The\nwinners of the qualifiers feature in the main bouts.
MID_EV13_065_m01_011: I have here the schedule and opponent for your first\nqualifier match, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_065_m01_035: <TLP>Match: First Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Gaia Brigade\nLeader: Zarcone\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}　
MID_EV13_065_m01_012: I see. Tell the Divine Sovereign that I understand.
MID_EV13_065_m01_013: Ah, there's more. To participate in the Heroic\nGames, you have to register a clan name.
MID_EV13_065_m01_014: That much I have decided already. You shall register\nus as Megaira's Beacon.
MID_EV13_065_m01_015: Oh, after the big lighthouse north of the royal\ncapital? Solid choice.
MID_EV13_065_m01_016: Especially since you work so hard to keep the people\nof Saramis on course.
MID_EV13_065_m01_017: Now, it won't be long before the first qualifying\nmatch. Please be patient.
MID_EV13_065_m01_018: Speaking of which...I have an update regarding your\nrequest for suitable warriors for the games.
MID_EV13_065_m01_019: As you asked, I have selected only the best,\nregardless of origin or status.
MID_EV13_065_m01_020: I am Lysander Kleitos. It's an honor to receive such\nan opportunity, Your Majesty!
MID_EV13_065_m01_021: I'll give my all in the hopes of living up to your\nexpectations.
MID_EV13_065_m01_022: Kleitos's son, are you? Your father saved many lives\nduring the War of Grania.
MID_EV13_065_m01_023: All warriors of Saramis know of his deeds. I hope\nthat you will honor his name here.
MID_EV13_065_m01_024: Hey. I'm Lilian. Y'know, Lilian Tabatha?
MID_EV13_065_m01_025: I'll do as good a job as you pay me for, so thanks for\nthe advance.
MID_EV13_065_m01_026: How dare you take that attitude with Her Majesty!\nShow some respect!
MID_EV13_065_m01_027: Eh, it's fine. She won't complain as long as I do good\nin the arena, right?
MID_EV13_065_m01_028: And I will, so there's no problem. Alright then,\nsee you folks around.
MID_EV13_065_m01_029: From under what stone did you unearth that one?
MID_EV13_065_m01_030: My sincere apologies, Your Majesty. I'll give her\na stern talking-to.
MID_EV13_065_m01_031: She said Tabatha, did she not? Bonaventure, would\nthat be the same Tabatha who...
MID_EV13_065_m01_032: I was wary of that myself, but Your Majesty did\ninstruct me to disregard origin and status.
MID_EV13_065_m01_033: Her skill, I assure you, is unimpeachable. Despite\nthe rather dispiriting rumors about her.
MID_EV13_065_m01_034: That is well, then. I look forward to seeing you all\nwork together in the games.
MID_EV13_101_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_101_m01_001: Bonaventure, what is this line for? The people seem\nunusually interested in it.
MID_EV13_101_m01_002: A fortune teller is casting bones and reading the\nresult. It's something of a new fad in this city.
MID_EV13_101_m01_003: Very interesting. As we have some free time, I shall\nsee for myself how it is done.
MID_EV13_101_m01_004: What would you like to know? I can divine on\nany subject.
MID_EV13_101_m01_006: I am curious about my prospects for victory. Divine\nthe winner of the Heroic Games for me.
MID_EV13_101_m01_007: Kun, or the "Weariness" hexagram. You will meet\nwith great difficulty. Victory is impossible.
MID_EV13_101_m01_008: Potential avenues are closed off for you. You won't\nsee this contest through to its end.
MID_EV13_101_m01_009: What did you say to me? Do you value your life?
MID_EV13_101_m01_010: Are you asking for a fight? I would win.
MID_EV13_101_m01_011: Believe what you will, but I carry the long-deferred\ndream of a million souls.
MID_EV13_101_m01_012: Oh? Are you a Mediator as well?
MID_EV13_101_m01_013: I do not mediate. I decree. Or did you not know you\naddress the queen of Saramis?
MID_EV13_101_m01_014: Saramis. I see. Then you are a child of Damascar,\nwhich means you and I are kin.
MID_EV13_101_m01_015: If we meet in the Heroic Games, I ask that\nyou forfeit.
MID_EV13_101_m01_016: That way we will not have to fight.
MID_EV13_101_m01_017: It's my responsibility to protect you, as kin. So please,\nconsider my request. I don't want to hurt you.
MID_EV13_101_m01_018: I've heard enough. Sorry for the waste of time.\nNever before have I paid to be so insulted.
MID_EV13_101_m01_019: This city is an endless parade of eccentrics. Though\nI suppose with a large enough population...
MID_EV13_101_m01_020: I believe it's been at least, oh, 30 years since I saw\nsuch an ancient form of divination.
MID_EV13_101_m01_021: It used to be practiced within Saramis too, but one\nrarely sees it performed nowadays.
MID_EV13_101_m01_022: And what did she mean by "kin"? She did not\nappear to be of the forest clans.
MID_EV13_101_m01_023: There was something about her... It felt strangely\nfamiliar to me.